                "At its core, crochet is the art of pulling yarn loops through other yarn loops using a notched hook. Each completed pass forms a stitch, and series of stitches form rows or rounds that build solid fabric. Understanding the three primary structural building blocks—chains, rows, and individual stitches—will make every pattern easier to follow.",
